<!--Blurb: Different answers to the riddles in SN 1:62.-->
<h2 class="h1">Craving<br/>
Taṇhā Sutta  (SN 1:63)</h2>
<div class="verse">
<pre>“By what	is the world led?
By what	is it dragged around?
What	is the one thing
	that has the all
	under its sway?”</pre>
<pre>“By craving 	is the world led.
By craving 	is it dragged around.
Craving 		is the one thing
	that has the all
	under its sway.”</pre>
</div><!--end verse-->
<p> See also: <a href="SN35_23.html" class="sutta-ref">SN 35:23</a>; <a href="SN35_82.html" class="sutta-ref">SN 35:82</a>; <a href="../AN/AN10_58.html" class="sutta-ref">AN 10:58</a></p>

      </div><!--end:sutta-->
